<section id="zero-knowledge" aria-labelledby="zk-architecture-heading" class="border-b border-slate-200/80 bg-white py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-blue-600">01 • Principle of Complete Privacy</p>
            <h2 id="zk-architecture-heading" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">
                We Cannot Read Your Passwords. And That Is by Design.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                PassKee is built on strict <strong>Zero-Knowledge</strong> end-to-end encryption. Your logins, cards, SSH keys, database credentials, and notes are encrypted and decrypted exclusively inside your browser. Data arrives on our servers as raw binary ciphertext (<code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-slate-800">bytea</code>) for which we never hold the key.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6">
                <div class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-blue-600 text-white text-base font-bold">
                    01
                </div>
                <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Argon2id Client KDF</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                    Your browser combines your <strong>Master Password</strong> and <strong>128-bit Emergency Secret Key</strong> with your 32-byte salt using <strong>Argon2id</strong> to derive a 256-bit Master Key in RAM.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6">
                <div class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 text-white text-base font-bold">
                    02
                </div>
                <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Zero-Leak Authentication</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                    Your Master Key never leaves your device. To authenticate, the client computes <code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">HMAC-SHA256(MasterKey, "auth_login")</code>, which the server hashes a second time with Argon2id.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6">
                <div class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-600 text-white text-base font-bold">
                    03
                </div>
                <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold text-slate-900">X25519 + AES-256-GCM</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                    Each user has a <strong>Curve25519 (X25519)</strong> keypair and a 256-bit Vault Key encrypted with AES-256-GCM. Every vault key is wrapped via ephemeral ECDH + AES-256-GCM with 12-byte random nonces.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6">
                <div class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-slate-900 text-white text-base font-bold">
                    04
                </div>
                <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold text-slate-900">15-Minute RAM Zeroing</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                    After 15 minutes of inactivity—or when you click <strong>Lock</strong>—PassKee executes <code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">CryptographicOperations.ZeroMemory</code> on your Private Key and Vault Key in RAM.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
